## KEY DATA RULES
- "(123)" means negative 123. Strip footnote markers (r/, p/, 3/).
- Check table headers: "(in millions)" vs "(in thousands)" vs "(in dollars)".
- FISCAL vs CALENDAR: FY pre-1977 = Jul–Jun. FY post-1977 = Oct–Sep. CY = Jan–Dec.
- Bulletin year ≠ data year. A 1941 bulletin often reports 1940 data.
- Match EXACT row labels. "National defense" ≠ "Total national security".
- Read ALL *_page_*.txt files if multiple exist.
- Percentages: write 15.3 not 0.153 or 0.1534.
- Multiple values: [x, y] format without units/commas.

## MATH FORMULAS (use python3 -c for all)
```python
pct_change = ((new - old) / old) * 100
cagr = (end/start) ** (1/n) - 1
geom_mean = (product) ** (1/n)  # or: from statistics import geometric_mean; geometric_mean([...])
arith_mean = sum(values) / len(values)
stdev = statistics.stdev(values)
pstdev = statistics.pstdev(values)
median = statistics.median(values)
range_val = max(values) - min(values)
```

